# Workflow

This page is how you develop a Rocci application from the source checkout.
Command flags live in the [CLI](/docs/reference/cli/). Repository automation
and local ops live in `rocci-ops` (`uv run rocci-ops`): CI helpers, site
package, and container sketches under `docker/`.

`rocci inspect FILE` prints components and source-map segments.

## Run the app

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/standalone/counter
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/standalone/counter --no-window
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/standalone/counter --no-live-reload
```

`--no-window` prints a URL; the HTTP origin is the same as the preview webview.
`--no-live-reload` pauses automatic refresh; watch still rebuilds.
`--log-handlers` prints matched routes.

## Preview and browse

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- view \
  examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci \
  --component Hello --arg name=Ada
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- browse examples/rocci/standalone/styling
```

`view` ignores HTTP declarations. `browse` is the component gallery.

## Inspect lowering

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- inspect examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- inspect --ast examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci
```

`inspect` always prints source-map segments. `--ast` adds the S-expression tree.

## Playground

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- playground examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci
```

WASM mode shows lowered Roc; it does not snapshot HTML. `--mode local` needs
the [install](/docs/install/) toolchain.

## Editors

Editor support is **current** in this repository. There is no Marketplace
install path yet. The server binary is `rocci-language-server`
(`cargo build -p rocci-rocdown-lsp`). The VS Code and Zed extensions are thin
LSP clients. Opening a `.rocci` file should show diagnostics and semantic
highlighting.

## Dev panel

In the preview window, open Dev. **Performance**, **Source**, and **Console**
are host tools. Console shows runtime lines and teed Roc stderr, not
`@component` logs.

| Moment | Work |
| --- | --- |
| Edit | Watch rebuilds the lowered module |
| Compile | Roc toolchain on generated source |
| Document GET | `@get:view` returns a full document |
| One-shot mutation | fragment HTML over SSE; Datastar morphs one tab |
| Live poll | authored `@get:live` path; unchanged HTML is skipped |

**Related:** [Diagnostics](/docs/reference/diagnostics/),
[Runtime](/docs/reference/runtime/).
